diff --git a/docs/chat-bots.md b/docs/chat-bots.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e9d7f09
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/chat-bots.md
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Chat bots
+
+Open **Account settings → Set up chat bots** to create a bot and copy its code.
+Members can manage the bots they create; administrators can manage all bots.
+Bots automatically join open rooms. Add them to closed rooms from the room's
+membership settings, just like any other member.
+
+Post a message by sending UTF-8 text as the request body. No browser session,
+JSON wrapper, or form fields are needed:
+
+```sh
+curl --fail-with-body --data-binary 'Deploy of v1.2.3 finished ✅' \
+  "https://chat.example.com/rooms/${ROOM_ID}/${BOT_CODE}/messages"
+```
+
+A successful request returns `201 Created` and a `Location` pointing to the
+message. The message link requires a signed-in room member. An invalid code
+returns `401`, an unknown or inaccessible room returns `404`, and a blank body
+returns `422`. Deleting a bot revokes its code and removes it from open and
+closed rooms without removing previously posted messages.
+
+Treat the bot code like a password. Keep it in your secret store, use HTTPS,
+and don't print the request URL in shell traces or CI logs. Campfire filters the
+code from its normal request logs, but any reverse proxy or access log in front
+of Campfire must also redact the code segment (or omit these paths).
diff --git a/lib/bot_message_request.rb b/lib/bot_message_request.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3768e6c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/lib/bot_message_request.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+class BotMessageRequest
+  CODE_PATH = %r{(/rooms/[^/?]+/)[^/?]+(/messages/?)(?=\?|\z)}
+
+  def self.redact_path(path)
+    path.sub(CODE_PATH, '\1[FILTERED]\2')
+  end
+
+  def initialize(app)
+    @app = app
+  end
+
+  def call(env)
+    if env["REQUEST_METHOD"] == "POST" && CODE_PATH.match?(env["PATH_INFO"])
+      # This endpoint takes raw text even when curl -d supplies a form content type.
+      # In particular, Rack must not interpret a message that starts with _method=.
+      env["CONTENT_TYPE"] = "text/plain"
+      env.delete("HTTP_X_HTTP_METHOD_OVERRIDE")
+    end
+
+    @app.call(env)
+  end
+
+  module FilteredPath
+    def filtered_path
+      BotMessageRequest.redact_path(super)
+    end
+  end
+end
